<div class="level">
  <div class="level-left">
    <h1 class="title level-item">DNS</h1>
  </div>
</div>

<p class="content">
  The internal resolver answers <code>A</code> records for your clients. The
  automatic per-client records appear below; add a static <code>A</code> record
  further down to layer extra names on top — a static record overrides an auto
  record with the same name. Only <code>A</code> records are served today.
  Everything this zone does not answer is forwarded — to the default upstream,
  or to a resolver you choose per domain under
  <a href="#conditional-forwarding">Conditional forwarding</a>.
</p>

<h2 class="title is-5">Automatic records</h2>
<p class="content is-small has-text-grey">
  Managed by the tool from your clients — one per client
  (<code>&lt;hostname&gt;.<%= @settings[:dns_domain] %></code>), plus the gateway and
  the <code><%= @settings[:dns_domain] %></code> apex. The bare
  <code>&lt;hostname&gt;</code> and reverse DNS also resolve. Add a static
  <code>A</code> record with the same name below to override one.
</p>
<table class="table is-fullwidth is-striped is-hoverable">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Name</th>
      <th>Type</th>
      <th>Value</th>
      <th>TTL</th>
      <th>Source</th>
      <th></th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <% @auto_rows.each do |row| %>
      <% overridden = @shadowed.include?(Naaf::Zone.normalize(row[:name])) %>
      <tr>
        <td><code><%= row[:name] %></code></td>
        <td><span class="tag"><%= row[:rtype] %></span></td>
        <td><code class="<%= "has-text-grey-light" if overridden %>"><%= row[:value] %></code></td>
        <td>60</td>
        <td><span class="tag is-light"><%= row[:source] %></span></td>
        <td>
          <% if overridden %>
            <span class="tag is-warning is-light">overridden by static</span>
          <% end %>
        </td>
      </tr>
    <% end %>
  </tbody>
</table>

<hr>

<h2 class="title is-5">Static records</h2>

<% if @rows.empty? %>
  <div class="notification">No static records. Client hostnames still resolve automatically.</div>
<% else %>
  <table class="table is-fullwidth is-striped is-hoverable">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Name</th>
        <th>Type</th>
        <th>Value</th>
        <th>TTL</th>
        <th></th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% @rows.each do |row| %>
        <tr>
          <td><code><%= row[:name] %></code></td>
          <td><span class="tag"><%= row[:rtype] %></span></td>
          <td><code><%= row[:value] %></code></td>
          <td><%= row[:ttl] %></td>
          <td>
            <form method="post" action="/dns-records/<%= row[:id] %>/delete">
              <%= csrf_tag("/dns-records/#{row[:id]}/delete") %>
              <button class="button is-small is-danger is-light" type="submit">Delete</button>
            </form>
          </td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
<% end %>

<hr>

<h2 class="title is-5">Add an A record</h2>
<form method="post" action="/dns-records">
  <%= csrf_tag("/dns-records") %>
  <div class="field is-grouped is-grouped-multiline">
    <div class="control is-expanded">
      <label class="label">Name</label>
      <input class="input" type="text" name="name" placeholder="service.<%= @settings[:dns_domain] %>" required>
    </div>
    <div class="control">
      <label class="label">IPv4 address</label>
      <input class="input" type="text" name="value" placeholder="10.8.0.10" required>
    </div>
    <div class="control">
      <label class="label">TTL</label>
      <input class="input" type="number" name="ttl" min="0" value="60">
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="field">
    <div class="control">
      <button class="button is-primary" type="submit">Add &amp; apply</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</form>

<hr>

<h2 class="title is-5" id="conditional-forwarding">Conditional forwarding</h2>
<p class="content is-small has-text-grey">
  Send one domain to a different resolver — a site's own DNS server, or a
  public one. The match is a suffix, dnsmasq-style and not an RFC 1034 wildcard:
  <code>example.com</code> matches <code>example.com</code> and
  <code>anything.example.com</code>, and the <strong>longest</strong> matching
  suffix wins. The zone above always wins over all of it, so a client's
  <code>.<%= @settings[:dns_domain] %></code> name is never forwarded. Names
  matching no suffix go to the default upstream
  (<code><%= h(@settings[:dns_upstream]) %></code>), set in
  <a href="/settings">Settings</a>. A reverse zone is ordinary DNS text here, so
  <code>1.168.192.in-addr.arpa</code> is a legal domain.
</p>

<% if @forwarders.empty? %>
  <div class="notification">
    No conditional forwarding. Every name this zone does not answer goes to
    <code><%= h(@settings[:dns_upstream]) %></code>.
  </div>
<% else %>
  <table class="table is-fullwidth is-striped is-hoverable">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Domain</th>
        <th>Resolver</th>
        <th>Source</th>
        <th>Notes</th>
        <th></th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% @forwarders.each do |row| %>
        <tr>
          <td><code>*.<%= h(row[:suffix]) %></code></td>
          <td>
            <code><%= h(row[:server]) %><%= (row[:port] == 53) ? "" : ":#{row[:port]}" %></code>
          </td>
          <td>
            <% if row[:site_id] %>
              <a href="/sites"><span class="tag is-light">site <%= h(row[:site_name]) %></span></a>
            <% else %>
              <span class="tag is-light">manual</span>
            <% end %>
          </td>
          <td><%= h(row[:notes].to_s) %></td>
          <td>
            <%# Site-owned rows are read-only here, the same treatment the
                automatic records get. The delete route filters on
                site_id IS NULL as well, so this is a presentation choice
                sitting on top of a guarantee rather than instead of one. %>
            <% if row[:site_id] %>
              <a href="/sites">managed on Sites →</a>
            <% else %>
              <form method="post" action="/dns-forwarders/<%= row[:id] %>/delete">
                <%= csrf_tag("/dns-forwarders/#{row[:id]}/delete") %>
                <button class="button is-small is-danger is-light" type="submit">Delete</button>
              </form>
            <% end %>
          </td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
<% end %>

<h2 class="title is-6">Forward a domain</h2>
<form method="post" action="/dns-forwarders">
  <%= csrf_tag("/dns-forwarders") %>
  <div class="field is-grouped is-grouped-multiline">
    <div class="control is-expanded">
      <label class="label">Domain</label>
      <input class="input" type="text" name="suffix" placeholder="example.com" required>
      <p class="help">A leading <code>*.</code> is accepted and stripped.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="control">
      <label class="label">Resolver</label>
      <input class="input" type="text" name="server" placeholder="9.9.9.9" required>
    </div>
    <div class="control">
      <label class="label">Port</label>
      <input class="input" type="number" name="port" value="53" min="1" max="65535">
    </div>
    <div class="control is-expanded">
      <label class="label">Notes <span class="has-text-grey">(optional)</span></label>
      <input class="input" type="text" name="notes" placeholder="corporate split-horizon">
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="field">
    <div class="control">
      <button class="button is-primary" type="submit">Forward &amp; apply</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</form>
